\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 
Missions introduce basic mechanics, give rewards, and eventually provide mission credits for the mission shop. Do not ignore them just because travel and gym training feel more important.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid14707570\charrsid14707570 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs28\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 GEORGE / BEGINNER MISSIONS
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 George's early missions teach city navigation, equipping weapons, attacking, training, and basic Crimes 2.0 use.
\par \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Beginner approach:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807\charrsid14707570 \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Complete tutorial missions when they appear.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Read each objective instead of guessing.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  If a mission gives energy, spend it deliberately on the intended task or gym training.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not buy expensive items for a beginner mission unless the mission specifically requires them.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid14707570\charrsid14707570 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs28\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 ANONYMOUS AND DUKE
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 
Anonymous unlocks around level 5 and introduces Duke contracts. Duke provides repeatable contracts, mostly built around attacking and related combat tasks.
\par \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Beginner approach:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807\charrsid14707570 \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Start Duke contracts once you can complete them without wasting excessive energy or meds.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not accept every contract blindly if it would force you into bad attacks, heavy medical use, or active-player drama.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Let contracts support your normal leveling and combat growth instead of replacing the level 15 plan.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid14707570\charrsid14707570 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs28\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 MISSION CREDITS
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 
Mission credits are a separate currency used in the mission shop. Six random rewards appear at a time, and unpurchased rewards rotate out after several days.
\par \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 High-value categories to watch:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807\charrsid14707570 \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Books
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Weapon attachments
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Special ammunition
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  High-quality weapons or armor when you understand their value
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs28\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Beginner rule:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 
Do not spend mission credits just because something is available. Mission credits are slow early, and bad purchases delay much better rewards later.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid14707570\charrsid14707570 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs28\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 BOOK WARNING
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Books are rare, non-tradeable, one-time-use items with 31-day effects. Many books are strongest when you can exploit the full month.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid8334701\charrsid14707570 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Before using a book, ask:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807\charrsid14707570 \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Can I log in consistently during the full effect window?
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do I have the money and energy plan to benefit from it?
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Is this book better saved for a future stage?
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Is this a passive book that is safe anytime, or a temporary multiplier that needs planning?
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid8334701 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Default beginner rule:
\par \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Save strong 31-day training, crime, travel, or combat books until you know how to use the full window.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807\charrsid14707570 
