\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\fs24\insrsid11282807\charrsid16613061 \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Beginner approach:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807\charrsid14707570 \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Buy the Racing License only when you are ready to race consistently.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Race official races for RP progress.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not spend RP in Class E.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  On class-up, build one useful car instead of spreading upgrades across many cars.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Save most RP earned in each class for the next class.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not casually swap tyres or gearing; some choices are costly to undo.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not buy expensive cars before you understand class, track, surface, and upgrade needs.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807 
