\par \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 Rules:
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Never give a Torn password to a third-party tool.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Use API keys, not login credentials.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Prefer limited-access or public-access keys when the tool does not need broader access.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Use separate keys for different tools when practical.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Remove old or unused keys.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Be cautious with tools that request more access than their purpose requires.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not paste API keys into public chats, faction channels, forum posts, screenshots, or shared doc\hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44 uments.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  Do not store API keys in visible notes, public spreadsheets, or scripts you share.
\par \bullet \hich\af44\dbch\af31505\loch\f44  If an extension, script, or site is no longer maintained, remove its key.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af44 \ltrch\fcs0 \f44\insrsid11282807 
